# What must never enter the Docker build context.
#
# This file is not an optimisation. Without it, a build from a working directory uploads the
# local obj/ folders, and those contain absolute NuGet paths from the machine that produced
# them — 'C:\Program Files (x86)\Microsoft Visual Studio\Shared\NuGetPackages' on Windows. The
# Linux build image cannot resolve that path and the publish step fails outright with
# MSB4018 / "Unable to find fallback package folder".
#
# It is also what keeps the context small. node_modules alone is 271 MB and is rebuilt inside
# the image anyway, so uploading it costs minutes per build and buys nothing.

# --- Build output and restore state, per the failure above ---
**/bin/
**/obj/
**/out/
**/publish/

# --- Front-end dependencies and build output ---
**/node_modules/
src/NexaOps.Web/dist/
**/.vite/

# --- Version control and CI ---
.git/
.gitignore
.github/
.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/

# --- Test and coverage artefacts ---
**/TestResults/
**/coverage/
**/*.trx

# --- Local configuration that must never reach an image ---
# appsettings.Development.json is excluded because it is the file most likely to acquire a real
# connection string on somebody's machine. Deployed configuration comes from Key Vault and the
# container app's environment, never from a file baked into the image.
**/appsettings.Development.json
**/appsettings.Local.json
**/*.user
**/.env
**/.env.*

# --- Documentation and infrastructure, which the image does not need ---
docs/
infra/
*.md
